{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-16982","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15115","text":"Skill 08 — Provider Implementation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-16984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15116","text":"How to build a provider that satisfies a [&] Protocol capability contract. Registration, conformance testing, and MCP transport binding."}]}],"id":"blk-16983","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-16985","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15117","text":"Why This Matters"}]},{"id":"blk-16986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15118","text":"Capabilities are interfaces. Providers are implementations. The protocol is only as useful as the providers that satisfy its contracts. This file teaches you how to build one."}]},{"id":"blk-16987","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15119","text":"The Provider Concept"}]},{"id":"blk-16988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15120","text":"A provider is a service that implements one or more capability contracts. The [&] Protocol ecosystem includes default providers:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-16990","spans":[{"id":"spn-15121","text":"Provider"}]},{"id":"blk-16991","spans":[{"id":"spn-15122","text":"Capabilities Provided"}]}],"id":"blk-16989","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-16992","spans":[{"id":"spn-15123","text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-16993","spans":[{"id":"spn-15124","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-15125","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15126","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.episodic"},{"id":"spn-15127","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15128","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-15129","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15130","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.attend"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16994","spans":[{"id":"spn-15131","text":"TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-16995","spans":[{"id":"spn-15132","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-15133","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15134","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.forecast"},{"id":"spn-15135","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15136","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.pattern"},{"id":"spn-15137","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15138","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.baseline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16996","spans":[{"id":"spn-15139","text":"GeoFleetic"}]},{"id":"blk-16997","spans":[{"id":"spn-15140","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.fleet"},{"id":"spn-15141","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15142","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.geofence"},{"id":"spn-15143","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15144","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.route"},{"id":"spn-15145","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15146","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.region"}]}],[{"id":"blk-16998","spans":[{"id":"spn-15147","text":"Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-16999","spans":[{"id":"spn-15148","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument"},{"id":"spn-15149","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15150","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.vote"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-17000","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15151","text":"But any MCP-compatible service can be a provider. The protocol is provider-agnostic by design."}]},{"id":"blk-17001","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15152","text":"Contract Conformance Requirements"}]},{"id":"blk-17002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15153","text":"To satisfy a capability contract, a provider MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-17003","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15154","text":"1. Implement all declared operations"}]},{"id":"blk-17004","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15155","text":"If the contract for "},{"id":"spn-15156","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-15157","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-15158","marks":["code"],"text":"detect"},{"id":"spn-15159","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15160","marks":["code"],"text":"enrich"},{"id":"spn-15161","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-15162","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-15163","text":" operations, the provider must implement all three."}]},{"id":"blk-17005","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15164","text":"2. Accept the declared input types"}]},{"id":"blk-17006","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15165","text":"Each operation specifies an "},{"id":"spn-15166","marks":["code"],"text":"in"},{"id":"spn-15167","text":" type. The provider must accept data conforming to that type."}]},{"id":"blk-17007","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15168","text":"3. Produce the declared output types"}]},{"id":"blk-17008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15169","text":"Each operation specifies an "},{"id":"spn-15170","marks":["code"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-15171","text":" type. The provider must return data conforming to that type."}]},{"id":"blk-17009","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15172","text":"4. Respect accepts_from / feeds_into"}]},{"id":"blk-17010","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15173","text":"The provider must accept input from the types listed in "},{"id":"spn-15174","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-15175","text":" and produce output consumable by the types in "},{"id":"spn-15176","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-15177","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-17011","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15178","text":"5. Expose operations via MCP transport"}]},{"id":"blk-17012","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15179","text":"Operations are invoked as MCP tools. The provider must respond to MCP tool calls over stdio or HTTP transport."}]},{"id":"blk-17013","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15180","text":"MCP Transport Binding"}]},{"id":"blk-17014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15181","text":"Providers expose their operations as MCP tools. The binding maps contract operations to MCP tool names:"}]},{"id":"blk-17015","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Contract operation    →    MCP tool name\n─────────────────────────────────────────\ndetect                →    detect_anomaly\nenrich                →    enrich_context\nlearn                 →    learn_observation"},{"id":"blk-17016","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15182","text":"Tool registration"}]},{"id":"blk-17017","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15183","text":"When the provider starts as an MCP server, it registers tools that correspond to its contract operations:"}]},{"id":"blk-17018","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"detect_anomaly\",\n      \"description\": \"Detect anomalous events in temporal data streams.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"data\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"number\" } },\n          \"streams\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"data\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-17019","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15184","text":"Resource registration (optional)"}]},{"id":"blk-17020","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15185","text":"Providers can also expose MCP resources for read-only state inspection:"}]},{"id":"blk-17021","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"resources\": [\n    {\n      \"uri\": \"provider://runtime/health\",\n      \"name\": \"Provider Health\",\n      \"description\": \"Runtime health status\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-17022","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15186","text":"Provider Registration"}]},{"id":"blk-17023","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15187","text":"To make a provider discoverable, register it in the capability registry."}]},{"id":"blk-17024","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15188","text":"Registry entry format"}]},{"id":"blk-17025","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"provider\": \"my-time-provider\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": [\"&time.anomaly\", \"&time.forecast\"],\n  \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n  \"command\": \"my-time-provider\",\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"contracts/v0.1.0/time.anomaly.contract.json\",\n    \"contracts/v0.1.0/time.forecast.contract.json\"\n  ],\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/org/my-time-provider\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-17026","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15189","text":"The registry is used by "},{"id":"spn-15190","marks":["code"],"text":"provider: \"auto\""},{"id":"spn-15191","text":" resolution and by the "},{"id":"spn-15192","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-15193","text":" command to verify that providers exist."}]},{"id":"blk-17027","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15194","text":"Testing Provider Conformance"}]},{"id":"blk-17028","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15195","text":"Contract validation"}]},{"id":"blk-17029","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15196","text":"Verify that your provider's MCP tool surface matches the declared contract:"}]},{"id":"blk-17030","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"# List your provider's tools\necho '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"tools/list\",\"id\":1}' | my-provider\n\n# Compare against the contract\nampersand validate-provider \\\n  --provider my-time-provider \\\n  --contract contracts/v0.1.0/time.anomaly.contract.json"},{"id":"blk-17031","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15197","text":"Integration testing"}]},{"id":"blk-17032","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15198","text":"Test that each operation accepts the declared input type and produces the declared output type:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-17034","spans":[{"id":"spn-15199","text":"Test"}]},{"id":"blk-17035","spans":[{"id":"spn-15200","text":"What to verify"}]}],"id":"blk-17033","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-17036","spans":[{"id":"spn-15201","text":"Input acceptance"}]},{"id":"blk-17037","spans":[{"id":"spn-15202","text":"Send each "},{"id":"spn-15203","marks":["code"],"text":"in"},{"id":"spn-15204","text":" type; verify no error"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17038","spans":[{"id":"spn-15205","text":"Output shape"}]},{"id":"blk-17039","spans":[{"id":"spn-15206","text":"Verify output matches "},{"id":"spn-15207","marks":["code"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-15208","text":" type"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17040","spans":[{"id":"spn-15209","text":"Wildcard compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-17041","spans":[{"id":"spn-15210","text":"Send output from "},{"id":"spn-15211","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.*"},{"id":"spn-15212","text":" provider; verify acceptance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17042","spans":[{"id":"spn-15213","text":"Error handling"}]},{"id":"blk-17043","spans":[{"id":"spn-15214","text":"Send invalid input; verify graceful error response"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17044","spans":[{"id":"spn-15215","text":"Side effects"}]},{"id":"blk-17045","spans":[{"id":"spn-15216","text":"Verify "},{"id":"spn-15217","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: true"},{"id":"spn-15218","text":" operations modify state"}]}],[{"id":"blk-17046","spans":[{"id":"spn-15219","text":"Idempotency"}]},{"id":"blk-17047","spans":[{"id":"spn-15220","text":"Verify "},{"id":"spn-15221","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: false"},{"id":"spn-15222","text":" operations are safe to retry"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-17048","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15223","text":"Common Implementation Patterns"}]},{"id":"blk-17049","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15224","text":"Pattern 1: Thin MCP wrapper"}]},{"id":"blk-17050","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15225","text":"Wrap an existing service (database, API, ML model) in an MCP server that maps contract operations to service calls:"}]},{"id":"blk-17051","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"MCP tool call → Provider → Existing service → Response → MCP result"},{"id":"blk-17052","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15226","text":"This is the simplest approach. Graphonomous wraps an Elixir/OTP application. A pgvector provider would wrap PostgreSQL."}]},{"id":"blk-17053","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15227","text":"Pattern 2: Multi-capability provider"}]},{"id":"blk-17054","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15228","text":"A single provider can satisfy multiple contracts. Graphonomous provides "},{"id":"spn-15229","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-15230","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15231","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.episodic"},{"id":"spn-15232","text":", "},{"id":"spn-15233","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-15234","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-15235","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.attend"},{"id":"spn-15236","text":" — all from one MCP server."}]},{"id":"blk-17055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15237","text":"Register each capability separately in the contract, but serve them from one process."}]},{"id":"blk-17056","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15238","text":"Pattern 3: Stateless operation provider"}]},{"id":"blk-17057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15239","text":"Some capabilities are stateless — they transform input without maintaining state. These are simpler to implement and test:"}]},{"id":"blk-17058","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Input → Transform → Output (no state)"},{"id":"blk-17059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15240","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-15241","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic: true"},{"id":"spn-15242","text":" flag in the contract signals this pattern."}]},{"id":"blk-17060","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15243","text":"Pattern 4: Provider with feedback loop"}]},{"id":"blk-17061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15244","text":"Providers with "},{"id":"spn-15245","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-15246","text":" operations accept outcome feedback and improve over time. This requires persistent state:"}]},{"id":"blk-17062","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Input → Process → Output\n                  ↓\n          Feedback → State update"},{"id":"blk-17063","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15247","text":"Mark these operations with "},{"id":"spn-15248","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: true"},{"id":"spn-15249","text":" in the contract."}]},{"id":"blk-17064","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-15250","text":"Checklist: Shipping a New Provider"}]},{"id":"blk-17065","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15251","text":"Choose which capability contracts to satisfy"}]}],"id":"blk-17066","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15252","text":"Implement all operations declared in each contract"}]}],"id":"blk-17068","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15253","text":"Build an MCP server that exposes operations as tools"}]}],"id":"blk-17070","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15254","text":"Write a registry entry for discoverability"}]}],"id":"blk-17072","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17075","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15255","text":"Test conformance against the contract schemas"}]}],"id":"blk-17074","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17077","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15256","text":"Publish the provider (npm, hex, crates.io, or standalone binary)"}]}],"id":"blk-17076","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-17079","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-15257","text":"Submit a PR to add your provider to the registry"}]}],"id":"blk-17078","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierayuzxfybgke6wqyuihvg4sbeb2yqjjxeylkkef62xl3rzoyvo76xa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}